  "notes": "The opening finishes the right-torsor argument by identifying a stabilizing self-homeomorphism with a deck transformation and applying Proposition 2. Corollaire 2 asserts contractibility of components of the finite étale mapping space. Corollaire 3 replaces a crossed-out torsor assertion by a finite-stabilizer statement for the unoriented Teichmüller group. Its stabilizers are identified with covering automorphism groups, and its orbits with isomorphism classes of covers of Y homeomorphic to X.\n\nTwo slanted marginal additions are retained: realization of every finite subgroup as a stabilizer, described as a “Th. profond et récent”, and finiteness of the orbit set, with fini doubly underlined. The realization statement is not proved or verified here; in particular this page does not explain its relation to the unramified restriction. The final bracket introduces the orientation-preserving subgroup and the sign product, with the previously omitted “resp. −”. Pencil page 7.\n\nFor connected finite-type anabelian surfaces, the finiteness remark is supported by the fixed degree d=χ_c(X)/χ_c(Y): finitely many homomorphisms from a finitely generated π₁(Y) to the finite symmetric group S_d give finitely many degree-d covers. This checks finiteness under those hypotheses; contractibility and realization are not re-proved.",
